# Canonical multi-node topology demo and cross-gait limitation case.
# Demonstrates:
# - walk and jog graph nodes with self-edges and directed cross-node edges;
# - node-local parameter domains and explicit gait-change transitions.
# Does not demonstrate:
# - a fully parameterized walk/jog controller;
# - jog interpolation or jog steering: jog is a fixed single-example node;
# - equal transition quality across same-gait and cross-gait edges.
#
# Walk parameters are normalized authored controls calibrated against measured
# turn rate. The jog parameter domain is the singleton [0, 0].
node walk 1
registration walk LeftAnkle LeftAnkle,RightAnkle 3 1
parameter_metric walk turn_rate
example walk 0.0 ../BVH/walkCurve.bvh
example walk 0.5 ../BVH/walkMoreCurve.bvh
example walk 1.0 ../BVH/walkTightCurve.bvh

node jog 1
registration jog LeftAnkle LeftAnkle,RightAnkle 3 0
example jog 0.0 ../BVH/jogCurve.bvh
expect jog spanned_axes 0

# D6 raw-sum thresholds, calibrated per directed edge.
edge walk walk
edge_config walk walk 225 250 8 40 17
edge walk jog
edge_config walk jog 450 500 8 20 19
edge jog walk
edge_config jog walk 300 350 4 40 23
edge jog jog
edge_config jog jog 80 100 4 20 29
